[0.014111, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m \u001b[1mcd /tmp/morning-recorded\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m \u001b[1mclaude -p --model claude-opus-5-5 \"Last night's order sync run said OK, but this morning some products have wrong stock. Find out why. The job runs with .venv/bin/python. Last night's run was recorded; the ormaos CLI is at .venv/bin/ormaos; run \".venv/bin/ormaos guide\" first.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[3.739435, "o", "\u001b[36m\u001b[1m> Bash\u001b[0m .venv/bin/ormaos guide; ls -la\r\n"]
[3.923656, "o", "\u001b[2m  ormaos: what happened inside a Python run, to read instead of guessing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  WHEN TO USE IT\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  - A Python program runs, and its output does not explain what it did: a job\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    that prints OK, an error that never shows, a result you cannot trace.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  - You want to see what ran: the project's calls with the shape of their\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    arguments, every exception (also the caught ones), the SQL statements,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m    files, subprocesses and HTTP requests.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.923758, "o", "\u001b[2m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  WHERE TO START\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  1. Record:  ormaos run -- <command>\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m     The command runs unchanged (same output, same exit code); its Python must\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ... 50 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[6.376422, "o", "\u001b[36m\u001b[1m> Bash\u001b[0m .venv/bin/ormaos list; .venv/bin/ormaos show; .venv/bin/ormaos exceptions last\r\n"]
[6.54203, "o", "\u001b[2m  1 recording in .ormaos, newest first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  r1  2026-11-26 16:14:35  exit 0  600.9ms  1 process, 240 calls, 6 exceptions (5 swallowed), 123 io  .venv/bin/python \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  job.py --source <str[3]>\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  next: ormaos show r1\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  r1 exit 0 in 0.60s: 1 Python process, 240 calls, 6 exceptions (5 swallowed, 0 uncaught)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.542145, "o", "\u001b[2m  command: .venv/bin/python job.py --source <str[3]>\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  swallowed 5x validate.SkuFormatError at job.py:57 in sync_orders, raised at validate.py:24  [r1:e1]\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  io: 123 events (sqlite 121, http 1, file 1)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  not collected: io: reads of the 1 file opened at fetch.py:26: opened for reading, and no `read` call by Python code \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  was seen on a file of that name: if it was read, that was inside C code (a file that is iterated, `for line in f`, \u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.542165, "o", "\u001b[2m  `csv.reader`)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  not collected: io: sockets, at fetch.py:60 (once): a socket was connected or bound there; sockets are not recorded, \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ... 11 more lines\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
